   "file": "THE_DOCUMENT_CLASS_TAXONOMY.md",
   "path": "D:\\MY-DOwnloads\\PLACE-papers\\phase1.5\\method\\THE_DOCUMENT_CLASS_TAXONOMY.md",
   "line": 14,
   "text": "**Tier K — Keystone-certified.** A document whose load-bearing claims are backed by a **machine-checked kernel terminal at a pin**, Gate-1-graded (DERIVES, or INTERFACES-with-a-named-premise). *Obligation:* every such claim states its **grade · terminal · pin**, and the axiom profile is written in full (\"the standard three axioms {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}\", or cleaner). *Citation rule:* **may be cited as certification** — the terminal, at its grade, is the warrant."
  },
  {
   "label": "the standard -- Tier C is never cited as certification",
   "tag": "STANDARD",
   "file": "THE_DOCUMENT_CLASS_TAXONOMY.md",
   "path": "D:\\MY-DOwnloads\\PLACE-papers\\phase1.5\\method\\THE_DOCUMENT_CLASS_TAXONOMY.md",
   "line": 16,
   "text": "**Tier C — Cluster-synthesis.** A document that **organizes** certified results into a cross-system picture, panel, map, or interpretation — asserting *relationships* not individually certified. *Obligation:* state the invariant it organizes on; flag any tuple/value that is a **coordinate, not an invariant**; carry the Gate-1b discipline (classification × certification is the invariant, not a shared tuple). *Citation rule:* **cite for orientation and organization — NEVER as certification of the relationships it draws.** This is the taxonomy's load-bearing rule."
  },
  {
   "label": "the standard -- the CATALOGOS borderline",
   "tag": "STANDARD",
   "file": "THE_DOCUMENT_CLASS_TAXONOMY.md",
   "path": "D:\\MY-DOwnloads\\PLACE-papers\\phase1.5\\method\\THE_DOCUMENT_CLASS_TAXONOMY.md",
   "line": 40,
   "text": "- **CATALOGOS** — a Tier-C synthesis that *contains* Tier-K terminal citations (the Lean-verified counts). It is **Tier C** (its cross-system claims are synthesis), but its individually-pinned terminal rows are K-grade. Read the panels as C, the pinned terminals as K."
